<div class="wp-block-group hk-panel hk-panel--prose"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-intro"} -->
<p class="hk-intro">These terms govern course enrolment, kit fulfillment, assessment rules, certificate validity, and cancellation policies for the Hakari Course.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-read","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group hk-read"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh">Enrolment, Kit Fulfillment, and Platform Access</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">By registering for the Hakari Course, you agree to these binding service terms. Enrolment is secured upon receipt of payment in EUR, with all published fees including statutory VAT. Practical training kits—including digital probe thermometers, calibration cups, wipes, and log pads—are dispatched within 5 working days of enrolment. Learners receive twelve months of platform access starting from their cohort's official Monday launch date. Course materials, video lessons, and digital resources are provided for individual educational use and may not be copied, broadcast, or redistributed without prior written consent from the Hakari food-safety school.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh">Examination Regulations, Resits, and Certification Validity</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">Certification requires completing the 40-question proctored online exam within 60 minutes and achieving a minimum score of 75 %. All enrolments include one free exam resit within 30 days of the first attempt. Any subsequent attempts incur an extra exam resit fee of €60. Certificates are issued digitally as verifiable PDFs within 2 working days of passing and remain valid for 3 years. Re-issuing an existing certificate or requesting a certified copy in a second language incurs a fee of €20. Hakari Course certificates verify training in Codex Alimentarius HACCP principles but do not confer statutory business licenses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh">Cancellation, Refund Policies, and Team Bookings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">A full refund is available if a cancellation notice is submitted in writing at least 14 days before the cohort start date. Following the cohort start date, a full refund remains available within 14 days, provided the learner has accessed fewer than 25 % of the published lessons. Beyond these thresholds, fees are non-refundable. Team enrolments of 5 or more learners from one organization qualify for the €330 seat rate and may be invoiced directly. Inquiries and notices must be sent to hello@hakari-course.example, with responses provided within one working day.</p>
